KZ3 patch 2039 (hooks D/E, RSX pass 39): keycap prompts.
rsx_keycaps.h (new, included by rsx_live_draw.c): recognises the game's two prompt atlases by an FNV-1a 64 hash
(HUD 1024x512 DXT5, menu 512x128 DXT5) and, while the last input came from the keyboard/mouse, uploads a copy
whose pad-button cells (the game's own ButtonIcon / ImageMap rectangles) hold keycaps with the bound key: a dark
rounded body with a light rim like the game's L1/R1 cells, the key name (text drawn by the exe's UI font through
rsx_keycaps_set_source), a mouse picture for Mouse1-3, a triangle for arrow keys, "WASD"-style labels on the stick
cells. BC3 blocks under the cells are decoded, drawn and re-encoded; nothing else changes.
rsx_live_draw.c: the DXT5 upload path applies it; texcache_t remembers the atlas kind and the device/bindings
signature it was drawn for, and a cache hit re-uploads (in place, patch 2035) when the signature changes.
cellPad.c: pad_kb_key_for_input(name, slot) for the lookups. KZ3_KEYCAPS=0 off; LD_KEYCAP_DBG=1 logs the
fingerprint of every candidate upload. Log: [keycap]. Host test: tools/smoke/test_keycaps.sh.

